 repeatedly  denied anything unusual was going on  as panic turned to confusion and  confusion turned to skepticism the  original Daily NK story issued a  correction it was actually based only on  a single unnamed source CNN changed its  headline to sound more cautious and the  previously mentioned tweet and post were  deleted for a week or so the media  boldly asserted he's either dead or  alive then on May 1st 20 days after his  last appearance Kim jong-eun returned  this time to inspect a fertilizer  factory outside Pyongyang in hindsight  it's no secret how these rumors spread  he had a procedure became he's in  critical condition after surgery became  he's dead through a series of sloppy  journalistic escalations because so many  outlets published the story people  thought there must be some truth to it  after all this is perhaps the easiest  rumor to sell who would doubt 5 foot 7  300-pound a chain-smoking kim jong hoon  the man who had a harder time planting a  tree in his 30s than his 65 year old  South Korean counterpart would have  health troubles of course nothing that  happened on May 1st or since precludes  the possibility of Kim having surgery  some medical experts argue a new small  mark seen on the leaders right wrist  could be a sign of a cardiovascular  procedure he was also seen using a golf  cart as he did after a six-week absence  in 2014  caused by a suspected ankle injury  although he has used the cart at other  times as well another theory suggests  Kim may have been hiding from an  outbreak of coronavirus pyongyang  residents have reportedly been rushing  to stock up at grocery stores  confounding the problem is the current  lack of foreigners in the country and  minimal travel across the Chinese border  making reliable sources difficult to  find we may never know why Kim jong-eun  disappeared what we do know is that the  North Korean government chose not to  report on or snap a photo of their  leaders whereabouts to  those three weeks whatever the cause of  the disappearance the strategic reason  for silence is simple after the world  finishes celebrating the death of a  brutal murderous dictator it realizes  the somehow even scarier potential  alternative the subsequent chaotic  struggle for control of its nuclear and  chemical weapons rumors of Kim's death  are an accidental reminder of how bad  things could be and how much stability  is worth so while recent events may have  only been a false alarm they invite a  very real question one day possibly any  day Kim Jong moon will die or be  replaced and when that happens who will  inherit the nuclear codes in its 71  years of existence only three people and  one family have ever ruled the  Democratic People's Republic of Korea  from the country's founding in 1948 kim  ill sung would stay in power for another  46 years until his death in 94 during  this time japan cycle through 21 prime  ministers britain xi and the u.s. nine  presidents the small Hermit Kingdom  would both outlive its Soviet Ally and  survive Chinese reform around the age of  60 the country's founder and then only  leader began planning his legacy first  considering his brother before deciding  on his son the North Korean dictionary  quietly changed its definition of  hereditary succession as a reactionary  custom of exploitative societies and  began distributing paintings depicting  the leader in a more loving fatherly  light for the next few decades the  favored eldest son Kim Jong Il began  climbing the party's ranks eventually  pronounced supreme commander of the  Korean People's Army in 1991 thanks to  this preparation when a heart attack  killed Kim il-sung in 1994 power was  smoothly inherited by his son becoming  the first hereditary transfer of power  in a communist country the question of  who would follow Kim jong-il was far  more complicated he first married on his  father's request in 1966 and had a  daughter two years later one year after  that they divorced and Kim  almost immediately and in secret found a  second woman with whom he had a son Kim  jong-nam three years later not knowing  of this second relationship or child Kim  jong-il's father instructed him to  remarry another woman he did and  together the couple had two daughters  finally a few years later he met a young  dancer with whom he had a daughter  yo-jong and two sons gyeong-cheol and  Jang hoon Kim jong-il kept each family  in separate walden residences in  pyongyang giving the children quiet and  very isolated lives where they would not  encounter each other when it came time  for boarding school Jeong Nam was sent  to Geneva while the youngest three went  to Bern what happened next is somewhat  disputed conventional wisdom says that  Kim jong-nam  as the eldest son was his father's  favorite and next in line for the throne  until May 2001 when he was caught  sneaking into Japan to visit Tokyo  Disney with a fake Dominican Republic  passport and Chinese name in truth the  Tokyo incident was likely just one more  straw on the camel's back  reinforcing what was already becoming  true in fact some doubt Disney was the  real reason for the trip or even  suggests the arrest was set up while Kim  Jong yams mother visited Pyongyang only  occasionally from her home in Moscow and  was said not to be particularly  ambitious Kim Jong Un's mother was  highly involved in political life  pushing behind the scenes for her son's  ascent to power seeing his side of the  family had lost favor the eldest son  lived an aimless life of parties in  Pyongyang until his father offered him a  deal get married and have a child and  you can leave North Korea which Kim  jong-nam  took moving with his family to Macau the  middle child meanwhile was considered  too quiet and unmotivated leaving only  the youngest kim jeong-hoon to be clear  was not the perfect candidate his mother  was born in Japan never legally married  to Kim jong-il and her sister had  defected still thanks to his mother's  maneuvering hoon was officially chosen  as successor about five months after Kim  Jong Il's near fatal stroke in 2008  after which she had trouble moving the  left side of his body  almost nothing was known about the then  roughly 25 year old dictator and waiting  who like his father slowly ascended the  party until December 17 2011 when Kim  jong-il also like his father died of a  heart attack  both times Outsiders watched the  transition first from a militant  revolutionary ideologue to an awkward  film nerd then to a basketball loving 28  year old with about three years of  experience and waited for the regime to  collapse each time they said the country  could not survive without the  personality behind the cult and each  time the transition was incredibly  smooth and there ten years long at some  point one must accept that for all their  villainous behavior the Kim family is  also extremely skilled strategically it  should come as no surprise then that as  of now there is no obvious next in line  which could present a serious threat to  the current leadership if tradition  continues as it tends to in North Korea  power will be inherited by one of Kim  Jong Un's male children two factors  however complicate this first of his  three reported children the oldest is  said to be only ten which let's hope is  far too young even by North Korean  standards second Kim Jong Un's physical  health is probably much worse than his  predecessors meaning there's a very real  chance he could die before any of his  children reach maturity which brings us  back to the family tree anyone with Kim  family blood according to the country's  culture and tradition is a potential  rival as evidenced by the assassination  of Kim jong-nam in 2017 while returning  to his home in Macau the eldest brother  was attacked and killed at a check-in  counter at Kuala Lumpur Airport carrying  a hundred and twenty thousand dollars in  cash he's suspected of being a CIA  informant and as evidenced by his 12  vials of antidotes a nervous one his son  Kim Han Seoul is currently in hiding and  would probably be extremely wise to  remain that way the most realistic  replacements however come from within  the country the most high-profile of  which is Kim jong-un sister kim yo-jong  when she first appeared in public at her  father's funeral so little was known  about her that some suspected she was  Kim Jong Un's wife since then she has  assumed the very public role of  essentially her brother's assistant she  can be seen standing behind him at  important meetings and handing him a pen  at signings many would recognize her  face from the 2018 Winter Olympics where  she made waves for standing during the  South Korean national anthem cheering  for the unified Korea flag and inviting  the president to meet with her brother  on one hand at the amount of power she  has accumulated and her physical  proximity to kim jong hoon is a clear  sign of trust but given that hoon had  his own uncle executed by firing squad  what looks like trust could just as  easily be doubt in her ability to pose a  threat while she does have the  all-important Kim family blood she would  likely struggle to gain support in the  North's very patriarchal culture making  her a valuable asset to the current  leadership her supposed father-in-law  the well-connected Cho Rong hae is  another possible contender as a member  of the party Standing Committee Central  Committee military commission and a  deputy of the Supreme People's Assembly  wrong hae is one of the most powerful  senior officials in the country although  he lacks the family blood and therefore  also the financial access he's had  decades to build and maintain a  coalition which could in theory  eventually be used to seize control that  leaves only kim gyeong-cheol the older  full brother of kim jong hoon Cheol  reportedly can be found in one of two  places in pyongyang where he plays  guitar or wherever eric clapton is  playing a concert  it would seem his father was right he  has no political ambitions or like all  of this so it's thought the trouble with  understanding North Korea is that so  much of what we know is based on stories  told by a select few insiders living  abroad people like Kenji Fujimoto  formerly the Kim family sushi chef who  watched Kim jong-un and his siblings  grow up with so little information on  which to go on few opportunities to  calibrate our understanding and North  Korea itself usually disinterested in  confirming or to  rumors the outside world faces a tough  dilemma it would be foolish to totally  disregard the few tidbits of information  we do have as unproven speculation but  it would also be foolish to accept them  wholeheartedly and risk being misled as  we saw happen with the recent reports of  Kim Jong Un's death the next time Kim  jong-eun disappears we may learn from  this mistake and quickly dismissed the  story and yet when he does eventually  disappear from the world for good that's  exactly how it will probably look when  Kim jong-il died in December 2011 the  world continued operating as usual  totally oblivious for 51 hours during  that time the South Korean president  flew to Tokyo met the Prime Minister and  flew back its defense minister was in a  meeting when the announcement was  finally made afterward the Obama  administration reluctantly admitted they  were quote largely bystanders as the  guard changed in this notoriously cruel  nuclear-armed nation as it turned out we  got lucky there was no chaotic struggle  for power and 25 million citizens didn't  come flooding through the Chinese border  next time no one knows for sure if like  me you're not busy managing the  succession of your dictatorship I'm  willing to bet you might have a little  extra time at the moment if you're going  to be stuck indoors why not make use of  that time to learn something new on  brilliant maybe you've always wanted to  learn programming brilliant has courses  to